      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(chat): preserve explicit current-source sends in Control UI history",
        "body": "Related: #104544\nRelated: #83494\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an agent could explicitly send a successful `message` tool reply to the exact current source conversation, while Control UI history omitted that delivered reply and showed only a later, different assistant final.\n\nThis PR addresses the explicit current-source `message` send slice of #104544. It does not address missing subagent lifecycle announcements, which are tracked separately in #105517.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nExplicit routes were excluded from message-tool history projection even when the resolved channel, account, target, and thread matched the current source conversation. The change adds a structured current-source route marker at the outbound owner and permits marker-backed successful explicit sends in the history projector.\n\nDry-run, suppressed, and explicit `ok: false` results remain excluded. Existing transcript delivery mirrors remain authoritative and are deduplicated.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers who receive an explicit agent reply in the current Telegram/Slack source conversation can now see the same reply in Control UI session history. Later assistant output no longer replaces that delivered message in the dashboard.\n\nCross-channel, cross-account, cross-target, and cross-thread sends remain excluded from the current session history.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact patch head: `8e1a56699c15d27847cf45065bb1305fa4868a11`\n- Exact-head Control UI proof: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/29226510248\n- Proof artifact: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/29226510248/artifacts/8269975305\n- Patch CI: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/29226510257\n- Exact-base upstream comparison: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/29226570970\n\nThe exact-head proof runs focused gateway/outbound regressions, projects a confirmed current-source tool result through the production history projector, and renders the resulting history in the real Control UI with Playwright. The uploaded screenshot shows the Telegram-delivered reply before a later, distinct final; the JSON artifact records rendered order `sourceIndex=0`, `laterIndex=1`.\n\nPatch-specific checks pass, including formatting, lint, production types, test types, LOC guard, Control UI history proof, gateway, agent tools, embedded agent, and the focused outbound regressions. The full matrix currently has two failures: the exact-base branch already contains a stale dead-export baseline, and the locale-sensitive Control UI approval timestamp test remains flaky. The linked exact-base comparison is included to classify those failures independently of this patch.\n\n## Risk And Rollback\n\nRisk is limited to read-time history projection and the structured result metadata used to prove an exact current-source route. The marker is emitted only after trusted channel/account/target/thread resolution, and projection continues to reject existing non-success indicators.\n\nRollback is a straight revert of this PR. No config, schema, transcript migration, or persisted data rewrite is introduced.\n\n## Documentation\n\nNo documentation change is needed. This restores consistency between an existing channel delivery path and the existing Control UI history surface without changing configuration or user-facing commands.\n",
